# Firebase

- Use the emulator for local work. Do not deploy rules or indexes to a live project from an agent session.
- Firestore holds documents. Realtime Database holds live location and presence only. Do not put prices in RTDB.
- Client writes to booking, payment, wallet, coupon, review aggregate, and verification fields are denied.
- Location writes: own node, own booking, gate open. The API maintains the gate.
- Chat messages are written by the API. Clients listen.
- Storage paths come from the server. Reject `..` and user-chosen absolute paths.
- Admin SDK is used only in the FastAPI adapter, never in Flutter.
- Every new collection needs a rules test and an index note in `docs/prd/09-domain-and-data-model.md` if the query is new.
- Map Firestore documents to domain entities inside the adapter. Widgets never see a `DocumentSnapshot`.

Detail: `docs/prd/09-domain-and-data-model.md`, `docs/prd/10-hybrid-backend.md`.
